<title>FRANCE: ADP export traffic up 1.4 pct in September.</title>
<headline>ADP export traffic up 1.4 pct in September.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>September 1996 export traffic from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 49,954 tonnes, up 1.4 percent on a year ago, Aeroports de Paris, (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>Traffic on the ADP's major export route, North America, fell by 1.3 percent on September 1995 to 13,528 tonnes while shipments to the Far East declined by 5.2 percent to 10,147 tonnes.</p>
<p>In contrast, shipments from CDG and Orly to the European Union rose by 22.9 percent to 6,410 tonnes.</p>
<p>The ADP's global export traffic in tonnes for September 1996, by region, with percentage change on September 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p>     Domestic		   3,834    up     0.7</p>
<p>     European Union	   6,410    up    22.9</p>
<p>     Non-EU Europe	    1,150    down   7.4</p>
<p>     North Africa		 911    up     7.1</p>
<p>     Sub-Saharan Africa     4,315    up     8.2</p>
<p>     North America	   13,528    down   1.3</p>
<p>     French territories     2,042    down  15.1</p>
<p>     Latin America	    2,684    up     3.4</p>
<p>     Middle East		4,933    up     3.4</p>
<p>     Far East		  10,147    down   5.2</p>
<p>     Total		     49,954    up     1.4</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
